# Trivy vulnerability suppressions for `Dockerfile.api` / `Dockerfile.console`
# runtime image (`gcr.io/distroless/nodejs22-debian13:nonroot`).
#
# Each entry MUST include:
#   - An `exp:YYYY-MM-DD` expiry date (Trivy honours this; after the date the
#     suppression silently turns into a no-op and the CVE re-fires).
#   - A short reason explaining WHY the fix is not actionable in this repo
#     right now (otherwise an audit reviewer cannot tell whether the entry is
#     load-bearing or stale).
#
# Audit cadence: nightly container-scan workflow runs against latest distroless
# digest. When upstream rebuilds the image with the patched libssl3 / etc.,
# Trivy stops reporting these CVEs and the entries become harmless. The expiry
# date is a self-cleaning safety net: if the rebuild slips by 30 days, the
# entry expires, the CVE re-fires, and the container-scan job goes red again so
# we re-evaluate.
#
# Do NOT add unfixed/MEDIUM/LOW entries here — the workflow already passes
# `ignore-unfixed: true` and only gates on CRITICAL/HIGH. This file is the
# CRITICAL/HIGH escape hatch for upstream-lag cases only.

# All CVE-2026-* for libssl3 are fixed in nodejs22-debian13:nonroot
# (libssl3 3.0.19-1). The suppressions below are no longer needed.
# Migrated to nodejs22-debian13:nonroot (fixed: 3.0.19-1) on 2026-06-05.

# Trivy DB lists fixed form-data versions (2.5.6, 3.0.5, 4.0.6), but none are
# published to npm as of 2026-06-16 (`pnpm view form-data versions --json`).
# Remove this once a fixed form-data release is available and the lockfile is
# bumped/overridden.
CVE-2026-12143 exp:2026-06-23

# undici WebSocket DoS via fragment count bypass (GHSA-vxpw-j846-p89q). Patched
# in undici >= 6.27.0 / >= 7.28.0 / >= 8.5.0. The dev-tooling chain
# `@expo/cli > undici@6.25.0` still ships the vulnerable 6.x because upstream
# `expo` (SDK 53 cadence) hasn't bumped yet. Production runtime uses
# `undici@7.28.0` via the #3642 override (Fastify stack), and the WebSocket
# client itself is not invoked by any prod code path. Tracked in
# `docs/04-governance/security/audit-exceptions.md` (Due date 2026-09-30).
CVE-2026-12151 exp:2026-09-30
